  "summary": "Olmsted Falls (Ohio) police added a fourth Flock license plate reader camera at Bagley Road and Brentwood Drive, two years after first deploying LPRs. Chief Odis B. Rogers described uses including warrants, Amber/Silver Alerts, locating a missing elderly person, and a recent arrest of a wanted person with a gun and drugs.",
  "key_quotes": [
    {
      "quote": "We're finding that we are getting consistent hits for various things -- and it's not just warrants, suspended licenses and the historically common law-enforcement things",
      "paragraph_idx": 4
    },
    {
      "quote": "Individually a $3,000 annual cost, Flock cameras are also located at the intersections of Columbia and Cook roads, Bagley and Lewis roads and Columbia and Sprague roads.",
      "paragraph_idx": 6
    },
    {
      "quote": "A lot of people don't understand this is not a speed camera and it doesn't write tickets",
      "paragraph_idx": 9
    }
  ],
